  "body": "Part of #992 (its \"Done means\": \"The milled `Bore` ride's axis entry gets the same reading or its own issue\").\n\nThe milled Bore ride (`machining2d::bore`, the `OpParams::Bore` arm of `operation::generate`) enters each hole on its axis (`Entry3D::Plunge`) and rings out to the wall. The Bore arm asks no centre-cutting law and does not read the stock the program ahead leaves standing, so a Bore with a cutter that is **not centre-cutting** (`Tool::center_cutting == false`) on an undrilled hole plunges that cutter into solid stock with no finding at generate, verify or the post gate - the same gap #992 closed for Thread (found while working #992; not reproduced with a test yet).\n\n**Fix sketch:** for a cutter that is not centre-cutting, read the prior grid under the hole's axis entry the way `operation::thread_entry::judge` (#992, PR stacked on #1005) does - the program ahead must have opened the cutter's own cylinder down to its lowest axis point - and refuse by name otherwise. A centre-cutting cutter keeps today's ride (or gets a ramp/helix entry; out of scope).\n\n**Done means:** a Bore with a non-centre-cutting end mill on an undrilled hole is refused by name; the same after a Drill at least the cutter's diameter generates; a centre-cutting cutter is unchanged; pinned by an app test.\n\nPriority note: P1 until reproduced; if a test confirms the plunge posts, it is crash-class and goes to P0.\n",
